\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6.1}{\ignorespaces Top-down overview of the shared stadium footprint: UP and DOWN tracks, the island station platform, carved river with a road and a railway bridge, tree line, and the two-train fleet (HUD shows the active zone, signal aspect, CAM state, sensor health, speed and camera mode). Captured from \texttt {capture\_double\_track.gd} under headless software rendering; the HUD \texttt {MQTT offline} flag is expected in capture mode where the broker is intentionally not connected.}}{27}{figure.caption.7}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6.2}{\ignorespaces Island station from above: mainly-top view showing platform modules, canopy/station building, both platforms and the two tracks. Captured from \texttt {capture\_station.gd}.}}{28}{figure.caption.8}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6.3}{\ignorespaces Island station at an oblique angle: platform modules and canopy silhouette against the parallel tracks and stadium corridor in the background. Captured from \texttt {capture\_station.gd}.}}{29}{figure.caption.9}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6.4}{\ignorespaces Wrong-line run at UP phase APPROACH: T3 still on DOWN, T1 approaching crossover A before any visible motion; note HUD hold progress. Captured from \texttt {capture\_crossover.gd}.}}{30}{figure.caption.10}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6.5}{\ignorespaces Wrong-line run at phase CROSS\_ENTRY/WRONG\_LINE: T1 blended onto DOWN at A -- visible train between the switch points with switch blades in motion. Captured from \texttt {capture\_crossover.gd}.}}{31}{figure.caption.11}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6.6}{\ignorespaces Wrong-line run completion (phase CROSS\_EXIT/CLEARANCE): T1 back on UP past B, T3 released from hold and both trains back under normal authority. Captured from \texttt {capture\_crossover.gd}.}}{32}{figure.caption.12}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6.7}{\ignorespaces Live meet execution with seed 4242: both trains near the island platform, one held, with the meet HUD showing phase, holder, chosen route and countdown. Captured from \texttt {capture\_meet.gd}.}}{33}{figure.caption.13}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6.8}{\ignorespaces Wokwi-style animal-assets sanity render: deer and elephant GLBs with articulated limbs posed near the track, plus the sensor hut and barrier kit. Captured from \texttt {capture\_animals.gd}.}}{34}{figure.caption.14}%
